WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.770
- All right, let's
finish up with something

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.810
people all over social
media are talking about.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.767
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.555
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.555 --> 00:00:07.560
(crowd applauding)

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.220
I love the idea of siblings
looking out for one another.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.020
And one Georgia woman wanted to help

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:13.980
her little brother out,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.990
after his engagement broke off,

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.490
by selling the ring.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.530
But when no one bid on social media

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.080
she decided to take a fresh approach.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.200
She reposted the ad with a few edits.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.217
It reads, "My super cute, super sweet

00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:29.647
"amazing firefighter brothers loss

00:00:29.647 --> 00:00:31.493
"can be a big win for you."

00:00:31.493 --> 00:00:32.970
(crowd softly whooping)

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.010
But here's what got everyone's attention.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:35.851
Here we go.

00:00:35.851 --> 00:00:37.390
(crowd loudly whooping)

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.430
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.900
They wanted more than the ring, I think.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.820
She also shared a few pictures

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.148
of her brother and his
firefighter friends.

00:00:44.148 --> 00:00:45.000
(crowd whooping)

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.890
Yeah, exactly, what are you selling here?

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.120
This is like those ads, you know,

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.515
were we're like, oh it's about a ring.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:50.670
(crowd laughing)

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.530
We have these siblings
on the line right now,

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.420
everybody say hi to Melissa and Patrick.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.326
What's up y'all?

00:00:55.326 --> 00:00:56.584
(crowd cheering)

00:00:56.584 --> 00:00:57.490
- Hey Kelly.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.830
- Hey.
(crowd applauding)

00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.663
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:59.663 --> 00:01:00.840
Melissa, how did you come up

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.010
with this approach for the ring?

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.200
You're awesome and should
get into marketing.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.533
- I think I missed my
calling as a madam actually.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.366
(crowd laughing)

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:08.670
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.190
Patrick was trying to
sell the blinking ring

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.660
and was unsuccessful,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.280
so I thought I'd give it a shot.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.720
It wasn't going well.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.230
So one night after a
couple of glasses of wine

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.040
I decided to try to
make it a bit more spicy

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.310
and more click-worthy,
I guess you could say.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.563
So I just put in the title,

00:01:28.563 --> 00:01:30.060
changed the ad up a little bit,

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.160
put in the title, look
at the last picture.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.010
And the last picture was of Patrick

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.710
and his very handsome friends

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.300
in their bathing suits at a party.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.780
So even though that did get some clicks,

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.470
it also backfired on me
'cause then they all said

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.640
we're not interested in the ring

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.880
but we are in the firemen.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.510
(all laughing)

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.830
- I love this.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.310
Patrick, did you know that
your sister was doing this?

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.210
- So I had no idea

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.940
she really was gonna be
doing it to this extent

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.950
but I did know she was
gonna be trying to ring

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.150
at a different angle.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.880
But yeah, we all thought it was hilarious

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.320
and we really just
wanted to sell the ring,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.020
but it got a lot more likes and clicks

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.610
I guess 'cause of all the pictures on it.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.960
- That's a good thing, man.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.910
So a lot of women were asking Patrick,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.550
if you were still
single, what is the word?

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.740
- No ma'am, I'm in a relationship now.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.690
Met a girl about seven or eight months ago

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.580
and everything's going great now.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.160
- I love that for you Patrick.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.040
(crowd applauding)

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.600
We wish you all the happiness.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.250
Thank you so much, Melissa, Patrick.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.450
Good luck selling that ring.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.932
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:31.932 --> 00:02:33.731
(crowd applauding)

00:02:33.731 --> 00:02:34.889
- [Patrick] Thank you.

00:02:34.889 --> 00:02:36.180
- And that's not all you two.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.760
Our season one partner,
Pilot Pen makers of G2,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.470
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.590
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like y'all.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.730
So they're gonna be writing you a cheque

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:45.630
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:46.550
How's that sound?

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:47.875
(crowd cheering)

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.024
- What?

00:02:49.024 --> 00:02:49.857
- What?

00:02:49.857 --> 00:02:50.706
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:50.706 --> 00:02:51.957
- Are you kidding me?

00:02:51.957 --> 00:02:53.820
- No, you gotta take that new girl out

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.110
you know, for dinner or something,

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.060
I don't know, just saying.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:57.893
And Melissa, you should get half.

00:02:57.893 --> 00:02:58.726
- [Patrick] Absolutely.

00:02:58.726 --> 00:02:59.559
- [Melissa] Oh my God.

00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:00.881
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:00.881 --> 00:03:01.714
- [Kelly] Alright.
- Thank you

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.670
- Thank you, guys.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.099
Y'all have such a great 2023.

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:04.932
(crowd cheering)
(crowd applauding)

00:03:04.932 --> 00:03:06.270
Thank you to all our guests today,

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.420
Salma Hayek, Tino, Dylan
Gilmer, Steven A. Smith,

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.710
Vincent, and Captain Bill Dell.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:13.610
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

